  "body": "## What changed\nThe cancellation transport waits for the cancel flag instead of a five-second clock.\n`HANG_GUARD` stops a hung test after 120 seconds.\nBoth cancellation tests now use `pump_until_started`.\nThis shared helper fails with a clear diagnostic if the transport never starts.\nThe existing cancellation assertions stay in place.\n\n## Cause\nThe old worker could stop before a slow UI thread sent the cancel flag.\nThe stall test also had an unbounded startup loop.\nIf the request ended before the transport started, that loop could wait forever.\n\n## Tests\nFinal head: `42a1a1da69c55b72b8417271980e04fbfd56a4f9`.\nBase: `upstream/main` at `034e91b8b78fa64989d18e1d5d17344531c4762c`.\nHost: `m3`, macOS (Darwin 25.6.0, arm64).\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib ai_chat::basic`: 10 of 10 sequential runs passed on `m3`. Each run had 7 passed tests and no failures (70 passes total). These are macOS results, not the requested Windows results.\n- `startup_wait_refuses_a_transport_that_never_started` pins the missing-start diagnostic. It passed.\n- Mutation proof: replacing the timeout assertion with a silent `break` made that pin fail (`test did not panic as expected`, exit 101). Restoring the assertion made it pass (1 passed, exit 0).\n- `cancel_after_long_ui_stall_still_reaches_blocked_worker` keeps the six-second stall pin.\n  The original PR showed that restoring the five-second worker clock made this pin fail. This round changed only the startup wait.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 10 steps completed; 9 passed and 1 failed.\n  The UI library had 1,682 passed, 7 failed, and 8 ignored tests.\n  All eight integration suites passed. The build passed.\n  The seven failures are the same host graphics failures recorded in the latest review.\n  The [latest review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4068#issuecomment-7175989065) reproduced them on upstream main. The error is `No adapter found`.\n  They are six `egui_app::report_tests` cases and `egui_app::tests::headless_run_succeeds`.\n  The quick gate is red; no green result is claimed.\n  Commands used `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`, `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`, and a four-job budget.\n  An earlier cache-wrapped build stalled. Automatic target seeding then introduced stale metadata.\n  A local dev-artifact cleanup and a cold build resolved the metadata errors.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed on the final head.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog` (`app suites: example_catalog`): 43 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored on the final head.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. `example_catalog` passed. No recorded program or catalog file changed. The diff changes only UI test files and this PR's decision record.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Review finding 2 remains open. The required ten Windows runs are unavailable on this host.\n  `bacon.local` and `lenny.local` resolve, but SSH denies authentication for `mikekinney`.\n  No Windows pass count is claimed. The upstream runner API returns HTTP 403. The fork has no registered runners.\n- Heavy lanes do not apply. The diff changes no motion, sim, post, geometry, or app code.\n- Screenshots do not apply. The diff changes no rendered UI.\n- No other golden suite is reached by this UI-test-only diff.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #4021\n",
